  "question": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\qt0002_a6f9b48dbde7.png\"/><br/>\nIn a series LCR circuit, the rms voltage across the resistor and the capacitor are 30 V and 90 V respectively. If the applied voltage is $50 \\sqrt{2} \\sin \\omega t$, then the peak voltage across the inductor is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "70 V",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "50 V",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$70 \\sqrt{2} \\mathrm{~V}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$50 \\sqrt{2} \\mathrm{~V}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint: $\\sqrt{30^2+\\left(90-V_{\\mathrm{L}}\\right)^2}=50$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{V}_{\\mathrm{L}}=50 \\mathrm{~V} \\\\\n& =\\left(\\mathrm{V}_{\\mathrm{L}}\\right)_{\\max }=50 \\sqrt{2} \\mathrm{~V}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  }
}